# FloodSight Himalaya — Backend API & Pipeline

FastAPI backend service for FloodSight Himalaya (Track B: mapping flood damage from satellite data).

## Purpose

The backend coordinates satellite data ingestion, geospatial flood detection pipelines, infrastructure damage assessments, and reporting services. It exposes REST API endpoints adhering to the data contract consumed by the frontend.

## Setup & Running

```bash
# 1. Create and activate a Python virtual environment (Python 3.11+)
cd backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows PowerShell: .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# 2. Install dependencies in editable mode with dev tools
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# 3. Configure environment variables (optional for local mock mode)
cp .env.example .env

# 4. Start the backend development server
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

## Running Tests & Linting

```bash
# Run the test suite
pytest

# Run linter
ruff check .

# Auto-format
ruff format .
```

## REST API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Status Code |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GET` | `/api/health` | Service health check | `200` |
| `POST` | `/api/analyze` | Start a new flood damage analysis | `202` (or `422` validation error) |
| `GET` | `/api/runs/{runId}/status` | Poll run lifecycle state (`queued`, `running`, `succeeded`, `failed`) and step progress | `200` (or `404`) |
| `GET` | `/api/runs/{runId}/result` | Retrieve full verified `RunResult` (GeoJSON layers, KPIs, cut-offs) | `200` (or `404`) |
| `GET` | `/api/runs` | List recent runs | `200` |
| `POST` | `/api/runs/{runId}/ask` | Copilot grounded Q&A (*501 until implemented*) | `501` |
| `GET` | `/api/runs/{runId}/report` | Situation report data (*501 until implemented*) | `501` |

## Permanent Scientific Integrity Rules

- **Validation-only sources**: Copernicus EMS (EMSR927), UNOSAT products, published damage maps, and post-event OSM edits are never used as pipeline inputs.
- **No invented claims**: Any metric or geometry not computed by real analysis code is explicitly marked as `mock`.
- **Area-agnostic**: No hardcoded case-study coordinates, dates, village names, or damage thresholds in reusable code paths.
